// base.kind's `when owner_post` handler, when the watcher's route answers Unclear (design-two-systems §13): the
// owner's words are given to no agent until the owner says whom they are for, drops them, or says them again. The
// surfaces show it at the chat's foot: "not given to anyone: WHY", a button per agent of AGENTS (every agent on the
// ticket, those the post names first), "everyone", "drop it"; the click is this step's answer, the owner's, logged and
// replayed like any answer. Typed words are not formed against it (paper-research N-807.p78; consult-3 p80, 2: a
// model's reading of "drop the wsl thing" withdrew posts of his): they are a post of their own, and the post waiting
// here is handed to every agent on the ticket. Again is kept for records from before, whose handlers run it; it hands
// the post to them all, and no longer drops it.
call clarify(text: Text, why: Text, agents: [Agent]) -> Send(to: [Agent]) | Drop | Again(text: Text)
  task clarify
  template
    Your message was not given to anyone: {{ why }}
    <<<
    {{ text }}
    >>>
    The agents on the ticket:{{ for a in agents }}
    - {{ a }}{{ end }}
    Answer one of:
    - Send(to): the message goes as it is to those agents. Only for a reply that says whom it is for and nothing
      more ("for fixer", "both of them").
    - Drop: forget the message: a reply that says to forget it, and nothing else ("never mind", "drop it", "forget it").
    - Again(text): the reply is the message said again, more clearly or changed. It replaces the message and is
      given to whom it is for. Any reply that says more than whom it is for is this.
